      "hints": [
        "For the second filter, the angle in Malus's law is the angle between its transmission axis and the polarisation emerging from the first filter.",
        "Write 5.2 = 5.7 cos²(α − 35°), find α − 35°, then use the stated range for α."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "After the first filter, the light is polarised along its 35° transmission axis and has intensity 5.7 W m⁻².",
        "The angle between the two transmission axes is α − 35°, so Malus's law gives 5.2 = 5.7 cos²(α − 35°).",
        "Solving gives α − 35° = 17°.",
        "Since α is greater than 35°, α = 35° + 17° = 52°."
      ],
